#. type: Title =
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "OCI Containers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:58
msgid ""
"The https://opencontainers.org/[Open Container Initiative], commonly "
"referred to as `+OCI+`, provides a vendor and OS-agnostic way to describe, "
"distribute, and run containers.  The OCI specifications provide these in a "
"way that can be used on many different operating systems, including "
"FreeBSD.  The underlying virtualization technology is still FreeBSD jails, "
"with the same feature set, but OCI tooling enables additional ways of "
"working, and constructing, container-based workloads.  https://"
"www.freebsd.org/releases/14.3R/announce/[14.3-RELEASE] and upwards, "
"including https://download.freebsd.org/snapshots/OCI-IMAGES/[snapshots], now "
"include OCI-compatible images, and the https://podman.io/[Podman] toolkit on "
"FreeBSD is ready to use them, on both amd64 and arm64 architectures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:60
msgid "For FreeBSD users familiar with jails, there is a loose analogy:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:62
msgid "FreeBSD's `+base.txz+` tarball is an example of a container image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:63
msgid ""
"the `+jail.conf+` file describes the desired container properties, or "
"`+Containerfile+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:64
msgid ""
"use the `+jail ..+` command to run a container, given a filesystem path, "
"with the `+podman+` suite of tools."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:68
msgid ""
"By importing this container stack, FreeBSD users both benefit from common "
"tooling, but also enjoy wide support across public and private container "
"registries, and container-specific tooling and services.  In the https://"
"download.freebsd.org/releases/OCI-IMAGES/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/aarch64/Latest/"
"[aarch64] and https://download.freebsd.org/releases/OCI-IMAGES/{rel-latest}-"
"RELEASE/amd64/Latest/[amd64] download directories, you'll see official OCI-"
"format images.  The naming may be a little confusing at first, but should "
"make sense once you start using them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:70
msgid ""
"The same images are also available through common public container "
"registries, including https://hub.docker.com/u/freebsd[Docker Hub], and "
"https://github.com/orgs/freebsd/packages[Github Container Registry], but for "
"the strongest chain of trust, you should fetch your image directly from "
"https://download.freebsd.org/releases[Official FreeBSD Releases], and import "
"them to your local system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:73
msgid ""
"Each image comprises a subset of a standard FreeBSD `+base.txz+` release "
"tarball, for various use cases, and the usual FreeBSD `+CHECKSUM.*+` files, "
"that can be verified against the PGP-signed release announcement.  This "
"gives a very strong chain of provenance, directly verifiable from the "
"FreeBSD release team."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"CHECKSUM.SHA256\n"
"CHECKSUM.SHA512\n"
"FreeBSD-{rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64-container-image-static.txz\n"
"FreeBSD-{rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64-container-image-dynamic.txz\n"
"FreeBSD-{rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64-container-image-runtime.txz\n"
"FreeBSD-{rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64-container-image-notoolchain.txz\n"
"FreeBSD-{rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64-container-image-toolchain.txz\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "Container Image Naming and Tagging"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:93
msgid ""
"FreeBSD's official container images are built from base system packages, "
"themselves built during the FreeBSD release process, and published to public "
"registries.  This guide explains how images are named and tagged, helping "
"you choose the right image for your needs, and ensuring you understand the "
"implications of each choice, as new images are published, and in some cases, "
"mutable tags are amended.  This naming convention aligns with the new base "
"system package naming scheme, giving clear provenance between container "
"images and the corresponding FreeBSD releases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "Available Image Types"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:98
msgid ""
"Five types of FreeBSD container images are available, for `+amd64+` and "
"`+aarch64+` architectures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "`+freebsd-static+`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:103
msgid ""
"The static image is intended as a base image, for a workload which is "
"entirely statically linked. It contains no libraries, nor binaries, just the "
"supporting files that most applications of this nature require."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:105
msgid "public TLS certificates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:106
msgid "minimal password file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:107
msgid "minimal termcap"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:108
msgid "timezone database"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:112
msgid ""
"Note that it has, by design, a lean footprint, to make a security compromise "
"of the container less useful to the attacker.  There's no UNIX shell, no "
"command-line tools, no dynamic libraries, nor package manager.  It is the "
"smallest image provided by the FreeBSD project."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "`+freebsd-dynamic+`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:120
msgid ""
"The dynamic image uses the static image as a parent layer, and supports "
"using shared libraries, including `+libc+`.  Most FreeBSD software should "
"run without issue with this image, with minor changes.  It doesn't have a "
"shell, rc system, nor a package manager.  These limitations are additional "
"security, making it awkward for attackers in a compromised container to move "
"laterally, or make use of tools that were never installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`+freebsd-runtime+`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:128
msgid ""
"Again, runtime builds on the preceding dynamic layer, and finally adds the "
"minimum that a user would expect - a UNIX shell, rc system, and the package "
"manager.  It is the ideal base image for porting existing applications with "
"a minimum of changes.  Users will need to include additional FreeBSD base "
"system libraries, as well as additional packages from the Ports tree.  This "
"is the closest to a typical FreeBSD system, including the man:pkg[8] tool, "
"allowing users to install, or do, almost anything, similar to a non-"
"containerised system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "`+freebsd-notoolchain+`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:133
msgid ""
"This base image contains almost all tools one would expect on a typical "
"FreeBSD system, excluding those that are directly hardware-related, and thus "
"not generally useful within a container, and the compiler and related "
"toolchain, as it is quite large."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "`+freebsd-toolchain+`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:140
msgid ""
"The Toolchain base image is the sum of all preceding images, including a "
"full compiler and toolchain.  It is generally possible to compile almost any "
"software for FreeBSD in the same way as a normal non-jailed FreeBSD system.  "
"All images follow a consistent naming pattern, derived from the FreeBSD "
"release they are based upon."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "Image Tag Structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immutable Tags"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:151
msgid ""
"Immutable tags never change and are ideal for production systems where you "
"need stability and predictability.  These are the most common tags used by "
"the release process.  They will not change, even after FreeBSD security "
"patches, or errata notices.  They are ideal for base images for software "
"deployments where a high degree of reproducibility is expected, even as a "
"trade-off against more pro-active security patching."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:153
msgid ""
"`+major.minor+` (e.g., `+14.4+`): Points to a specific FreeBSD RELEASE "
"version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:154
msgid ""
"`+major.minor.pX+` (e.g., `+14.4p1+`): Points to a specific patch level of a "
"RELEASE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:155
msgid ""
"`+major.snapYYYYMMDDHHMMSS+` (e.g., `+16.snap20260325035941+`): a snapshot "
"build with timestamp"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mutable Tags"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:160
msgid ""
"Mutable tags are updated over time and are ideal for production, or CI/CD "
"systems that always want the latest updates, but still wish to align with "
"FreeBSD ABI compatibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:162
msgid ""
"`+major+` (e.g., `+15+`) will always be the latest support RELEASE version "
"along the 15.x stable ABI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:165
msgid ""
"`+major.snap+` (e.g., `+15.snap+`) follows the latest developer snapshot "
"along the 15.x stable ABI train, will often be in advance of official "
"releases, and carries a risk of breakage, incompatibility, or other "
"unanticipated issues.  This is the most mutable tag, and should be used with "
"caution.  They are exactly the same as using FreeBSD's STABLE or CURRENT "
"snapshots, as they use those images as their source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:166
#, no-wrap
msgid "When to Use Each Tag Type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:168
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Production"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:171
msgid "Use immutable tags to ensure your environment stays consistent:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:173
msgid "`+freebsd-runtime:15.0+` - pinned to FreeBSD 15.0-RELEASE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:175
msgid ""
"When security patches are released, you must explicitly rebuild or update "
"with a new image tag."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:176
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Continuous Integration and Development"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:179
msgid "Use mutable tags to automatically get the latest updates:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:181
msgid ""
"`+freebsd-runtime:15+` - always the latest official RELEASE in the 15.x "
"series"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:184
msgid ""
"These additional mutable tags will follow the regular published snapshots of "
"FreeBSD STABLE and CURRENT.  Use these if you want to test against what "
"subsequent future releases of FreeBSD may contain, and accept occasional "
"breakage or unanticipated changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:186
msgid ""
"`+freebsd-runtime:14.snap+` - always the latest build from 14-STABLE branch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:187
msgid ""
"`+freebsd-runtime:15.snap+` - always the latest build from 15-STABLE branch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:188
msgid ""
"`+freebsd-runtime:16.snap+` - always the latest build from 16-CURRENT branch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "Official Registry Locations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:193
msgid ""
"Architecture-independent images can be downloaded and directly imported into "
"your own registry from the https://download.freebsd.org/releases[Official "
"FreeBSD Releases] site, or alternatively, pulled from the FreeBSD project's "
"https://hub.docker.com/u/freebsd[Docker Hub], or https://github.com/orgs/"
"freebsd/packages[GitHub Container Registry]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:195
msgid ""
"Both https://hub.docker.com/_/alpine/[Alpine Linux] and the https://"
"hub.docker.com/_/debian/[Debian] project publish tagged and mutable images, "
"using similar approaches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction to Podman"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:200
msgid ""
"The Podman suite comprises three main tools and a number of supporting ones:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:202
msgid ""
"https://podman.io/[podman] is a daemonless container engine using docker-"
"compatible commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:203
msgid "https://buildah.io/[buildah] generates OCI formatted container images"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:204
msgid ""
"https://github.com/containers/skopeo[skopeo] works with remote OCI image "
"registries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:206
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preparing the System for Podman Containers"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:211
msgid ""
"If running commands over SSH, or in a similar remote session, use "
"man:screen[1], man:tmux[1], or similar to avoid losing the connection while "
"restarting the firewall."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:214
msgid ""
"If ZFS is not available, switch to UFS storage and skip the ZFS commands "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:219
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# sed -I .bak -e 's/driver = \"zfs\"/driver = \"vfs\"/' \\\n"
"    /usr/local/etc/containers/storage.conf\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:222
msgid "Otherwise, create the container storage dataset:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:227
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# zfs create -o mountpoint=/var/db/containers zroot/containers\n"
"# zfs snapshot zroot/containers@empty\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:230
msgid "The File Descriptor filesystem is required:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:234
#, no-wrap
msgid "# mount -t fdescfs fdesc /dev/fd\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:237
msgid ""
"Podman uses FreeBSD's packet filter to forward container ports to the host "
"network:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:242
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# test -c /dev/pf || kldload pf\n"
"# sysctl net.pf.filter_local=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:245
msgid ""
"Amend `+/etc/sysctl.conf+` and `+/etc/fstab+` as appropriate, to make these "
"changes permanent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing Podman"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:250
msgid ""
"Only the `+sysutils/podman-suite+` meta-package is required, but if the "
"additional package:emulators/qemu-user-static[] package is installed, it "
"becomes possible to build or test images for other architectures such as "
"`+arm64+` on an `+amd64+` host."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:254
#, no-wrap
msgid "# pkg install -r FreeBSD -y podman-suite emulators/qemu-user-static\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:257
msgid ""
"Integrate changes from `+/usr/local/etc/containers/pf.conf.sample+` into `+/"
"etc/pf.conf+`, setting egress macros appropriately, then restart the "
"firewall:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "# service pf restart\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:265
msgid ""
"The packages install a number of template configuration files, none of which "
"need to be edited immediately.  Review and amend these as needed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:277
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# pkg list buildah podman conmon \\\n"
"    ocijail containers-common \\\n"
"    containernetworking-plugins \\\n"
"    | grep /etc/\n"
"/usr/local/etc/containers/containers.conf.sample\n"
"/usr/local/etc/containers/policy.json.sample\n"
"/usr/local/etc/containers/registries.conf.sample\n"
"/usr/local/etc/containers/storage.conf.sample\n"
"/usr/local/etc/containers/pf.conf.sample\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:280
#, no-wrap
msgid "Importing and Running Containers"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:285
msgid ""
"At present, all Podman containers on FreeBSD must run as root, as FreeBSD "
"jails require this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:288
msgid ""
"With the necessary tools and firewall rules in place, the officially "
"published images can be fetched from https://download.freebsd.org/releases/"
"OCI-IMAGES/[FreeBSD Releases], for https://download.freebsd.org/releases/OCI-"
"IMAGES/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/aarch64/Latest/[aarch64] or https://"
"download.freebsd.org/releases/OCI-IMAGES/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/amd64/Latest/"
"[amd64] as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:290
#, no-wrap
msgid "Importing FreeBSD OCI Images"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:293
msgid ""
"It is simplest to pull images directly from a public container registry, but "
"for the strongest chain of trust, download them from https://"
"download.freebsd.org/releases[FreeBSD.org] directly, and verify the "
"checksums against the PGP-signed release announcement."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:303
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# export OCIBASE=https://download.freebsd.org/releases/OCI-IMAGES/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/amd64/Latest\n"
"# podman load -i=$OCIBASE/FreeBSD-{rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64-container-image-static.txz\n"
"Getting image source signatures\n"
"Copying blob 44defc6cee2e done   |\n"
"Copying config 5921c62e76 done   |\n"
"Writing manifest to image destination\n"
"Loaded image: localhost/freebsd-static:{rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64\n"
msgstr ""

