"Writing manifest to image destination\n"
"Loaded image: localhost/freebsd-toolchain:{rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:334
#, no-wrap
msgid "Listing Images"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:345
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman images\n"
"REPOSITORY                    TAG                   IMAGE ID      CREATED       SIZE\n"
"localhost/freebsd-toolchain   {rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64  b927c11b2e8d  13 days ago   660 MB\n"
"localhost/freebsd-notoolchain {rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64  086572f35cc9  13 days ago   152 MB\n"
"localhost/freebsd-runtime     {rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64  90c493675429  13 days ago   34.1 MB\n"
"localhost/freebsd-dynamic     {rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64  33427d59f990  13 days ago   14.5 MB\n"
"localhost/freebsd-static      {rel-latest}-RELEASE-amd64  5921c62e76c1  13 days ago   2.92 MB\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:348
msgid ""
"Note that the image IDs are reproducible each time, and the `+IMAGE_ID+` "
"column matches the hashes reported when importing the images."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:350
#, no-wrap
msgid "Listing Layers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:353
msgid ""
"It is possible to show the layers that comprise an image, demonstrating how "
"the `+runtime+` image has three components, each one a layer in its own "
"right:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:364
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman image tree ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:14.2\n"
"Image ID: c5f3e77557a9\n"
"Tags:     [ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:14.2]\n"
"Size:     35.07MB\n"
"Image Layers\n"
"├── ID: cd53fb07fb66 Size: 5.449MB Top Layer of: [ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-static:14.2]\n"
"├── ID: a01d37f7777b Size:  10.4MB Top Layer of: [ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-dynamic:14.2]\n"
"└── ID: 36b0c80ca1f7 Size: 19.21MB Top Layer of: [ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:14.2]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:367
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using Public Registries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:371
msgid ""
"While the most secure provenance is downloading from https://"
"download.freebsd.org/releases[Official FreeBSD Releases], there are two "
"public container registries managed by the FreeBSD Release and Cluster Admin "
"teams.  The images from both registries are identical, but provide a simpler "
"and more container-friendly workflow."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:373
msgid "https://hub.docker.com/u/freebsd[Docker Hub]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:374
msgid "https://github.com/orgs/freebsd/packages[GitHub Container Registry]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:376
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fetching Containers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:379
msgid "Images can be fetched from a public registry using `+podman pull+`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:389
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman pull ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-notoolchain:{rel-latest}\n"
"Trying to pull ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-notoolchain:{rel-latest}...\n"
"Getting image source signatures\n"
"Copying blob 711cf0d3c0ef done   |\n"
"Copying config 086572f35c done   |\n"
"Writing manifest to image destination\n"
"086572f35cc90b1a1d2b7904b63e8a849071b4ba89b15492f6da47a802372aa2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:392
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running a Container"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:397
msgid ""
"Use `+podman run+` to start a container.  The `+-it+` flags allocate an "
"interactive terminal, and `+--rm+` removes the container when it exits.  If "
"no command is specified, the image's default entrypoint is used:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:402
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-notoolchain:{rel-latest}\n"
"# exit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:405
msgid "A specific command can be given as well:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:410
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-notoolchain:{rel-latest} uname -a\n"
"FreeBSD c0038de70651 {rel-latest}-RELEASE FreeBSD {rel-latest}-RELEASE releng/{rel-latest}-n283562-96841ea08dcf GENERIC amd64\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:414
msgid ""
"As the container image does not include the kernel, man:freebsd-version[1] "
"shows different results for the running kernel versus the installed "
"userland.  In this example, a {rel-latest-previous}-RELEASE container runs "
"on a {rel-latest}-RELEASE host:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:422
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-notoolchain:{rel-latest-previous} /bin/sh\n"
"# freebsd-version -ru\n"
"{rel-latest}-RELEASE\n"
"{rel-latest-previous}-RELEASE\n"
"# exit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:425
#, no-wrap
msgid "Useful Variations and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:429
msgid ""
"Almost all of the `+podman run ...+` parameters also apply to `+podman "
"build+`.  Refer to the man:podman-run[1] and man:podman-build[1] manual "
"pages for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:431
msgid ""
"Use the `+--rm+` flag to have ephemeral containers clean themselves up "
"afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:433
msgid "Use `+podman images -a+` to show all downloaded images:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:439
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman images -a\n"
"REPOSITORY                       TAG            IMAGE ID      CREATED      SIZE\n"
"ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime  {rel-latest}   90c493675429  2 weeks ago  34.1 MB\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:442
msgid "Use `+podman ps -a+` to see running containers:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:448
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman ps -a\n"
"CONTAINER ID  IMAGE                                          COMMAND  CREATED        STATUS        NAMES\n"
"3123623bef9b  ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest}   /bin/sh  4 minutes ago  Up 4 minutes  admiring_brattain\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:451
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:454
msgid ""
"Podman sets a number of default environment variables in each container:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:463
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-notoolchain:{rel-latest} /usr/bin/env\n"
"container=podman\n"
"TERM=xterm\n"
"PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin\n"
"HOME=/root\n"
"HOSTNAME=60bae3343e6b\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:467
msgid ""
"The `+HOSTNAME+` is set to the container ID by default.  It can be "
"overridden with `+--hostname+`, which is useful when the application inside "
"the container needs a stable or meaningful hostname."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:469
msgid "Arbitrary environment variables can be passed in with `+--env+`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:475
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run --env FOO=BAR -it --rm ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest}\n"
"# echo $FOO\n"
"BAR\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:478
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mounting Files and Volumes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:482
msgid ""
"Both files and volumes can be passed into containers using `+--volume+`.  "
"For example, the `+runtime+` image does not contain man:which[1]:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:488
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest}\n"
"# which\n"
"/bin/sh: which: not found\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:491
msgid "It can be mounted into the container from the host:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:498
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm --volume /usr/bin/which:/usr/bin/which \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest}\n"
"# which which\n"
"/usr/bin/which\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:503
msgid ""
"For a lean image such as `+freebsd-static+`, mount the existing man:pkg-"
"static[8] from the host to bootstrap man:pkg[8] inside the container.  "
"Sharing the host's package cache via `+--volume /var/cache/pkg+` avoids re-"
"downloading packages that have already been fetched, which is particularly "
"useful when building multiple containers.  The `+--no-hosts+` flag prevents "
"mounting `+/etc/hosts+`, which would otherwise interfere with package "
"upgrades."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:507
msgid ""
"Sharing the package cache only works when the host and container run the "
"same FreeBSD major version, as packages are version-specific."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:522
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm \\\n"
"    --env ASSUME_ALWAYS_YES=true \\\n"
"    --no-hosts \\\n"
"    --volume /usr/local/sbin/pkg-static:/bin/pkg-static \\\n"
"    --volume /var/cache/pkg \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-static:{rel-latest}\n"
"# pkg-static bootstrap -r FreeBSD\n"
"Bootstrapping pkg from pkg+https://pkg.FreeBSD.org/FreeBSD:14:amd64/latest, please wait...\n"
"Verifying signature with trusted certificate pkg.freebsd.org.2013102301... done\n"
"[fd343e182fa5] Installing pkg-2.1.2...\n"
"[fd343e182fa5] Extracting pkg-2.1.2: 100%\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:525
msgid ""
"Files and directories from the host can also be mounted into containers:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:533
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm \\\n"
"    --volume /etc/fstab:/etc/fstab \\\n"
"    --volume /tmp:/var/tmp \\\n"
"    --volume /tmp \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:536
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspecting Image Contents"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:539
msgid ""
"To list all files in any image, including minimal images with no shell or "
"tools, export the container filesystem and list its contents:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:543
#, no-wrap
msgid "# podman export $(podman create --rm ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-static:{rel-latest} /) | tar tf -\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:547
msgid ""
"The container images do not include man:pkg[8] itself, but man:pkg-static[8] "
"can be mounted from the host to query the installed base system packages.  "
"Use `+pkg info -q+` to list package names, or `+pkg info -ql+` to show all "
"files owned by packages:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:575
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run --rm \\\n"
"    -v /usr/local/sbin/pkg-static:/pkg \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest} /pkg info -q\n"
"FreeBSD-audit-lib-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-bzip2-lib-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-certctl-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-clibs-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-fetch-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-kerberos-lib-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-libarchive-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-libcasper-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-libexecinfo-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-libucl-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-mtree-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-ncurses-lib-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-openssl-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-openssl-lib-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-pam-lib-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-pkg-bootstrap-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-rc-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-runtime-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-xz-lib-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-zlib-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-zoneinfo-{rel-latest}\n"
"FreeBSD-zstd-lib-{rel-latest}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:578
msgid ""
"When the host and container run different FreeBSD major versions, man:pkg[8] "
"detects the ABI by inspecting `+/bin/sh+` inside the container, and will "
"warn about the mismatch:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:589
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm \\\n"
"    --env ASSUME_ALWAYS_YES=true \\\n"
"    --no-hosts \\\n"
"    --volume /usr/local/sbin/pkg-static:/usr/sbin/pkg \\\n"
"    --volume /var/cache/pkg \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:14.4 /bin/sh\n"
"# pkg bootstrap\n"
"pkg: Warning: Major OS version upgrade detected.  Running \"pkg bootstrap -f\" recommended\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:592
msgid ""
"For images without `+/bin/sh+`, such as `+freebsd-dynamic+`, man:pkg-"
"static[8] cannot detect the system ABI at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:594
#, no-wrap
msgid "Networking and Name Resolution"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:597
msgid ""
"By default, the Podman suite of tools will use man:mount_nullfs[8] to mount "
"`+/etc/resolv.conf+` and a modified `+/etc/hosts+` from the jail host, as "
"well as a `+.containerenv+` file in `+/var/run+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:599
msgid ""
"This hosts file will conflict with base system package upgrades, so it is "
"advised to skip this during `+podman build+` runs, but leave it enabled "
"during production deployment:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:604
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run --dns 1.2.3.4 ...\n"
"# podman build --no-hosts ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:608
msgid ""
"The `+--dns+` flag specifies a custom DNS server instead of mounting `+/etc/"
"resolv.conf+` from the host.  The `+--no-hosts+` flag prevents mounting `+/"
"etc/hosts+` from the host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:610
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building Custom Images"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:613
msgid ""
"Custom images can be built directly from tarballs (for example those from "
"man:poudriere[8], or official release tarballs), from existing tagged "
"images, or bootstrapped from man:pkg[8]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:615
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building from Tarballs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:620
msgid ""
"A custom image can be made from any FreeBSD root filesystem tarball using "
"man:podman-import[1].  The tarball can be an official release `+base.txz+`, "
"one produced by man:poudriere-image[8], or your own custom tarball.  The "
"final tagged image can be pushed to registries, modified, and used for "
"further image creation."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:633
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman import --os freebsd \\\n"
"    --arch amd64 \\\n"
"    --message 'Import FreeBSD {rel-latest}-RELEASE base.txz' \\\n"
"    https://download.freebsd.org/releases/amd64/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/base.txz\n"
"Downloading from \"https://download.freebsd.org/releases/amd64/{rel-latest}-RELEASE/base.txz\"\n"
"Getting image source signatures\n"
"Copying blob 3768988b151c done   |\n"
"Copying config 332bec83a4 done   |\n"
"Writing manifest to image destination\n"
"sha256:332bec83a428efa6c9f7d1f8b3fbd589c5613d938dca7da5125240c89f4f3dcd\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:635
#, no-wrap
msgid "# podman image tag 332bec83a428 localhost/freebsd-base:{rel-latest}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:639
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman image ls\n"
"REPOSITORY              TAG   IMAGE ID      CREATED        SIZE\n"
"localhost/freebsd-base  {rel-latest}  332bec83a428  5 minutes ago  715 MB\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:642
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building from Containerfiles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:647
msgid ""
"Images can be built using a `+Containerfile+`, similar to a Dockerfile.  In "
"most cases, the `+freebsd-notoolchain+` image is the most convenient base, "
"as it includes nearly all standard system tools.  For leaner containers, "
"start from `+freebsd-static+`, `+freebsd-dynamic+`, or `+freebsd-runtime+` "
"as appropriate, and add only what is needed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:657
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Containerfile\n"
"FROM ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-notoolchain:{rel-latest}\n"
"RUN env ASSUME_ALWAYS_YES=yes IGNORE_OS_VERSION=yes pkg bootstrap -r FreeBSD\n"
"RUN pkg update\n"
"RUN pkg upgrade -y\n"
"RUN pkg clean -y\n"
"ENTRYPOINT /bin/sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:660
msgid "Build the image with man:podman-build[1]:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:666
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman build --no-hosts --squash \\\n"
"    -t localhost/freebsd-base:{rel-latest} \\\n"
"    -f ./Containerfile\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:669
msgid "Further images can be layered on top:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:677
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Containerfile.webserver\n"
"FROM localhost/freebsd-base:{rel-latest}\n"
"RUN pkg install -y lang/python3\n"
"RUN pkg clean -y\n"
"ENTRYPOINT /usr/local/bin/python3 -m http.server\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:684
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman build --no-hosts \\\n"
"    -t localhost/python-www:{rel-latest} \\\n"
"    -f ./Containerfile.webserver\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:688
msgid ""
"Run the web server in the background with `+--detach+`, and use `+-p+` to "
"map a host port to the container port.  In this example, the container "
"listens on its default port 8000, which is mapped to port 8888 on the host:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:692
#, no-wrap
msgid "# c=$(podman run --detach --rm -p 8888:8000 localhost/python-www:{rel-latest})\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:696
msgid ""
"The port mapping uses man:pf[4] redirect rules.  These rules redirect "
"traffic arriving over the network, so the mapped port must be accessed from "
"another host, or via the host's network-facing IP address:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:704
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ fetch -v http://172.16.2.10:8888/\n"
"resolving server address: 172.16.2.10:8888\n"
"requesting http://172.16.2.10:8888/\n"
"remote size / mtime: 784 / 0\n"
"fetch.out                                              784  B 3791 kBps    00s\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:707
msgid ""
"To access the container directly from the host, use the container's own IP "
"on its listening port:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:717
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman inspect -f '{{.NetworkSettings.IPAddress}}' $c\n"
"10.88.0.91\n"
"# fetch -v http://10.88.0.91:8000/\n"
"resolving server address: 10.88.0.91:8000\n"
"requesting http://10.88.0.91:8000/\n"
"remote size / mtime: 784 / 0\n"
"fetch.out                                              784  B   25 MBps    00s\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:724
msgid ""
"Port mappings via `+-p+` are handled by man:pf[4] redirect rules and only "
"apply to traffic arriving over the network.  Traffic originating from the "
"jail host itself to `+localhost+` or `+127.0.0.1+` will not be redirected.  "
"From the host, use the container's IP address directly instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:727
#, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced Usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:730
#, no-wrap
msgid "Daemonising Podman"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:733
msgid "FreeBSD's Podman implementation provides two man:rc[8] services:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:735
msgid ""
"The `+podman+` service runs at boot and ensures that all containers marked "
"with `+restart-policy=always+` are started."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:736
msgid ""
"The `+podman_service+` service runs the https://docs.podman.io/en/latest/"
"_static/api.html[Podman API service], providing a REST API and listening on "
"`+/var/run/podman/podman.sock+` by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:738
msgid "Enable them as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:746
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# sysrc podman_enable=YES\n"
"# sysrc podman_service_enable=YES\n"
"# sysrc podman_service_flags='--time 0'\n"
"# service podman start\n"
"# service podman_service start\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:749
msgid ""
"Containers that should restart automatically after a host reboot must be run "
"with the `+--restart=always+` option:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:753
#, no-wrap
msgid "# podman run --detach --restart=always my-image\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:756
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running Linux Containers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:759
msgid ""
"It is possible to run many Linux container images using FreeBSD's Linux "
"emulation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:770
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# service linux onestart\n"
"# podman run --rm --os=linux docker.io/alpine cat /etc/os-release | head -1\n"
"Trying to pull docker.io/library/alpine:latest...\n"
"Getting image source signatures\n"
"Copying blob 4abcf2066143 done   |\n"
"Copying config 05455a0888 done   |\n"
"Writing manifest to image destination\n"
"NAME=\"Alpine Linux\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:775
msgid ""
"Linux containers that depend on systemd, expect to be PID 1, or rely on "
"Linux-specific kernel interfaces may not work correctly under FreeBSD's "
"Linux emulation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:778
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running a Local Registry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:783
msgid ""
"A registry is a web server for storing and sharing OCI images.  The https://"
"freshports.org/sysutils/docker-registry[sysutils/docker-registry] port "
"provides a simple registry suitable for local development or a small "
"organisation.  https://zotregistry.dev/[Zot Registry] is a more "
"comprehensive modern alternative."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:798
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# pkg install -r FreeBSD sysutils/docker-registry\n"
"# zfs create zroot/var/db/registry\n"
"# chown -R www:www /var/db/registry\n"
"# sysrc docker_registry_enable=YES\n"
"# sysrc docker_registry_user=www\n"
"# sed -i '' -E -e 's,rootdirectory:.+,rootdirectory: /var/db/registry,' \\\n"
"    /usr/local/etc/docker-registry/config.yml\n"
"# touch /usr/local/etc/docker-registry/htpasswd\n"
"# chown -R root:www /usr/local/etc/docker-registry/config.yml \\\n"
"    /usr/local/etc/docker-registry/htpasswd\n"
"# chmod 0640 /usr/local/etc/docker-registry/config.yml \\\n"
"    /usr/local/etc/docker-registry/htpasswd\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:801
msgid ""
"A sample configuration for `+/usr/local/etc/docker-registry/config.yml+`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:827
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"version: 0.1\n"
"log:\n"
"  fields:\n"
"    service: registry\n"
"storage:\n"
"  cache:\n"
"    blobdescriptor: inmemory\n"
"  filesystem:\n"
"    rootdirectory: /var/db/registry\n"
"http:\n"
"  addr: :5000\n"
"  secret: <random-secret>\n"
"  headers:\n"
"    X-Content-Type-Options: [nosniff]\n"
"auth:\n"
"  htpasswd:\n"
"    realm: basic-realm\n"
"    path: /usr/local/etc/docker-registry/htpasswd\n"
"health:\n"
"  storagedriver:\n"
"    enabled: true\n"
"    interval: 10s\n"
"    threshold: 3\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:830
msgid "Start the registry and verify it is running:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:835
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# service registry start\n"
"# curl -u admin:passwd http://localhost:5000/v2/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:840
msgid ""
"It is recommended to serve the registry over TLS, behind a reverse proxy "
"such as nginx or haproxy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:843
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synchronising Registries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:847
msgid ""
"It is possible to synchronise official FreeBSD images into a local registry "
"using `+skopeo+`.  The following example replicates all FreeBSD-related "
"images from https://hub.docker.com/u/freebsd[Docker Hub] to a local registry:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:856
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# sync.yml\n"
"docker.io:\n"
"  images:\n"
"    freebsd/freebsd-static: []\n"
"    freebsd/freebsd-dynamic: []\n"
"    freebsd/freebsd-runtime: []\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:865
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ skopeo sync --src yaml --dest docker --all sync.yml cr.example.net/freebsd\n"
"INFO[0000] Processing repo                               repo=freebsd/freebsd-static\n"
"INFO[0000] Querying registry for image tags              repo=freebsd/freebsd-static\n"
"...\n"
"INFO[0771] Synced 42 images from 3 sources\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:868
msgid ""
"So long as the credentials in `+/root/.config/containers/auth.json+` are up "
"to date, root access is not required to sync images."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:870
#, no-wrap
msgid "Working with Container Registries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:874
msgid ""
"Registries generally require authentication for push operations, and "
"optionally for pull.  Credentials are saved in `+/root/.config/containers/"
"auth.json+` by default after login:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:880
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman login ghcr.io -u username\n"
"Password:\n"
"Login Succeeded!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:883
msgid "Images can then be pushed to a registry:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:892
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman push localhost/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest} \\\n"
"    docker://ghcr.io/example/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest}\n"
"Getting image source signatures\n"
"Copying blob bbacfdfbe140 done   |\n"
"Copying config 786f2592a8 done   |\n"
"Writing manifest to image destination\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:895
msgid "Public images can be pulled without authentication:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:899
#, no-wrap
msgid "# podman pull ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:902
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building Container Images from Sources"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:906
msgid ""
"The FreeBSD release tooling provides an `+oci-release+` target to build the "
"necessary images for `+podman load+` to use.  It requires building world, "
"kernel, and base system packages first, so this can take a while."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:908
msgid "The following example builds `+arm64+` images:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:919
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/src \\\n"
"    && make TARGET_ARCH=aarch64 TARGET=arm64 -s -j32 buildworld \\\n"
"    && make TARGET_ARCH=aarch64 TARGET=arm64 KERNCONF=GENERIC -s -j32 buildkernel \\\n"
"    && make TARGET_ARCH=aarch64 TARGET=arm64 KERNCONF=GENERIC -s -j32 packages \\\n"
"    && cd ./release \\\n"
"    && make TARGET_ARCH=aarch64 TARGET=arm64 -j32 -s clean \\\n"
"    && make KERNCONF=GENERIC TARGET_ARCH=aarch64 TARGET=arm64 WITH_OCIIMAGES=yes \\\n"
"      -s oci-release\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:922
msgid "And similarly for `+amd64+`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:933
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/src \\\n"
"    && make TARGET_ARCH=amd64 TARGET=amd64 -s -j32 buildworld \\\n"
"    && make TARGET_ARCH=amd64 TARGET=amd64 KERNCONF=GENERIC -s -j32 buildkernel \\\n"
"    && make TARGET_ARCH=amd64 TARGET=amd64 KERNCONF=GENERIC -s -j32 packages \\\n"
"    && cd ./release \\\n"
"    && make TARGET_ARCH=amd64 TARGET=amd64 -s -j32 clean \\\n"
"    && make KERNCONF=GENERIC TARGET_ARCH=amd64 TARGET=amd64 \\\n"
"      WITH_OCIIMAGES=yes -s oci-release\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:936
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-Architecture Testing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:940
msgid ""
"The `+emulators/qemu-user-static+` package allows testing container images "
"built for other architectures.  After installing the package, enable and "
"start the service to register image activators for all emulated "
"architectures:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:946
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# pkg install emulators/qemu-user-static\n"
"# service qemu_user_static enable\n"
"# service qemu_user_static start\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:949
msgid ""
"Then run an `+arm64+` image on an `+amd64+` host by mounting the appropriate "
"QEMU binary:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:956
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run -it --rm --arch=arm64 \\\n"
"    -v /usr/local/bin/qemu-aarch64-static:/usr/local/bin/qemu-aarch64-static \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:14.snap uname -a\n"
"FreeBSD 73d4049d10b2 14.2-RELEASE-p1 FreeBSD 14.2-RELEASE-p1 GENERIC arm64\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:959
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:962
#, no-wrap
msgid "Package Upgrades and Mounted Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:966
msgid ""
"Podman mounts `+/etc/resolv.conf+` and `+/etc/hosts+` into containers using "
"man:mount_nullfs[8].  These mounts can cause errors during man:pkg[8] "
"operations with messages such as `+Cross-device link+`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:970
#, no-wrap
msgid "pkg: Fail to rename /etc/.pkgtemp.hosts.VeIDrHM0sKN5 -> /etc/hosts:Cross-device link\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:973
msgid "To avoid this, use `+--no-hosts+` and `+--dns+` flags:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:978
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run --no-hosts --dns 1.1.1.1 -it --rm \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest} /bin/sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:981
#, no-wrap
msgid "Checking Networking"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:985
msgid ""
"Start with the firewall rules from `+/usr/local/etc/containers/"
"pf.conf.sample+`.  Test connectivity step by step from within a container:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:993
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# podman run --no-hosts --dns 1.1.1.1 \\\n"
"    --env ASSUME_ALWAYS_YES=1 \\\n"
"    -it --rm \\\n"
"    ghcr.io/freebsd/freebsd-runtime:{rel-latest} \\\n"
"    /bin/sh\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:999
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# route show 1.1.1.1\n"
"   route to: 1.1.1.1\n"
"destination: default\n"
"    gateway: 10.88.0.1\n"
"  interface: eth0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1004
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# ping -c 3 10.88.0.1\n"
"PING 10.88.0.1 (10.88.0.1): 56 data bytes\n"
"64 bytes from 10.88.0.1: icmp_seq=0 ttl=64 time=0.083 ms\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1009
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# ping -c 3 1.1.1.1\n"
"PING 1.1.1.1 (1.1.1.1): 56 data bytes\n"
"64 bytes from 1.1.1.1: icmp_seq=0 ttl=60 time=0.920 ms\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1012
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# fetch -v http://1.1.1.1/\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1014
#, no-wrap
msgid "# pkg -dd bootstrap -r FreeBSD\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1020
msgid ""
"If man:ping[8] fails, check the firewall rules for blocked ICMP.  If "
"man:fetch[1] fails, check the firewall rules for blocked TCP on ports 80 and "
"443.  If man:pkg[8] fails but ICMP and TCP work, this may be a fragmentation "
"or MTU problem.  Add `+set reassemble yes no-df+` to `+/etc/pf.conf+` and "
"restart the firewall."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1022
msgid ""
"For debugging blocked packets, enable `+log+` on all block rules in `+/etc/"
"pf.conf+` and use man:tcpdump[1] on the man:pflog[4] device:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1027
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# service pflog onerestart\n"
"# tcpdump -vvveni pflog0 icmp or net 10.88.0.0/16\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1030
#, no-wrap
msgid "MTU Consistency"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1034
msgid ""
"Ensure MTU values are consistent across the primary network interface, the "
"container bridge, and the container itself.  Mismatched MTU values can cause "
"packet fragmentation and connectivity failures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1037
msgid ""
"In the following example, `+vtnet0+` has MTU 9000, but the bridge and "
"containers have MTU 1500.  In general, align the internal layout to match "
"the external network:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1042
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# ifconfig vtnet0 mtu 9000\n"
"# ifconfig cni-podman0 mtu 9000\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1045
msgid "Inside the container:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block - 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1049
#, no-wrap
msgid "# ifconfig eth0 mtu 9000\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/containers/_index.adoc:1052
msgid ""
"The bridges and epairs used by Podman are ephemeral and will need to be "
"configured for each bridge creation and each container.  In some cloud "
"environments, adding `+set reassemble yes no-df+` to `+/etc/pf.conf+` may "
"also be required."
msgstr ""
